  {
   "id": "commit:c0078cf487b06b1fc70501e4",
   "kind": "Commit",
   "label": "5a59e76e Make tf_gnns agent benchmarks ",
   "title": "Make tf_gnns agent benchmarks pass by improving user docs\n\nBenchmarks now pass 8/8 under ollama/qwen3.8 with the packaged\ntf-gnns-user-docs skill. The main changes:\n\n- Expand agent_skill references: multi-graph batching, subgraph\n  extraction with edge_trimming_mode, assign_global check_shape,\n  GraphNetMLP with globals and explicit sizes, factory config with\n  composite aggregation and eval_tensor_dict/graph_tuple_eval parity,\n  SparseGCN edge weights and dtypes, documented GCNv2 ValueError\n  boundaries.\n- Add Environment/Agent Workflow guidance to SKILL.md so agents use\n  the uv project env and the docs tool instead of probing the\n  environment or reading library source.\n- Tighten the suite agent_prompt (read the matching topic, write the\n  solution immediately, avoid env spelunking) and raise task timeouts\n  to 600s.\n- Run validation commands with uv run python; add agent_docs CLI,\n  API index generator, docs tests, and lazy package-root exports.\n- Ignore agent_benchmark_results/.\n",
   "time": "2026-09-13T23:56:57+00:00",
