  {
   "id": "commit:eb7c7f054684688f2b1c9fdb",
   "kind": "Commit",
   "label": "5042738d Restructure agent docs concept",
   "title": "Restructure agent docs concept-first; fix GraphNetMLP global contract; shift benchmark params\n\nConcept-first topic pages: every reference page now leads with How It\nWorks, Decision Guide, Parameter Key Facts, Boundaries & Gotchas, and a\nMinimal Skeleton before Rules/API Signatures/Output Contract, with\nexamples moved to a final Example Gallery. Agent_docs gains a --concepts\nextraction mode and the SKILL.md and benchmark suite agent_prompt now\ndirect agents to read concepts first and treat examples as reference,\nnot templates.\n\nDocs accuracy fixes: GraphNetMLP always builds a global block and fails\nwithout global_attr + repetition keys (verified against models/\ngraphnet.py); the no-global path is GraphNetMPNN_MLP only. Example\nGallery now shows reading object-graph edge widths via edge_tensor.\n\nAPI index: generator now unions root and submodule __all__ but keeps a\nsubmodule name only when the reference docs mention it (GCNv2 added,\nmaybe_patch_ld_library_path_for_tensorflow excluded), and filters\nunderscore-prefixed names.\n\nBenchmark shifts: tasks 09-14 parametrize so copy-pasting doc examples\nfails (units/widths/cores/reps/training paths all diverge from the docs).\nTrace rules flag examples-before-concepts retrieval and /tmp probe\nscripts. New reference solutions verified for all six shifted tasks.\n",
   "time": "2026-09-14T11:37:27+00:00",
   "props": {
